WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.510
- The Trump administration
is considering stimulus aid

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.920
for oil and gas producers

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.370
as oil prices plummet.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.080
Wisconsin's Republican leaders

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.320
are suing over the Democratic
governor's lockdown order.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.350
People stuck at home worldwide
have been a boon for Netflix,

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.473
adding nearly 16 million new subscribers.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.600
Hi, I'm Jason Bellini
with the latest reporting

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.350
on the coronavirus crisis
from The Wall Street Journal.

00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:30.620
- The energy business
is very important to us.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.700
- [Jason] As oil prices have collapsed,

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.190
the Trump administration
is weighing stimulus aid

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.410
for oil and gas companies.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.800
People familiar with the
matter tell The Journal the aid

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.330
would come in exchange for
government ownership stakes

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:46.220
in companies or their crude reserves.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.480
This plan is one of several
options on the table

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.120
and faces long odds given Democrats

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.030
will likely oppose using stimulus funds

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.850
to help the oil industry.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.970
Separately, the president
also said he would support

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.730
a $484 billion aid package

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.590
for small businesses and hospitals.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.010
It's moving to the House

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.560
after the Senate passed it Tuesday night.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.810
Republican law makers in
Wisconsin filed an injunction

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.050
targeting Governor Tony Evers' order

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.840
for businesses to close

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.433
and Wisconsinites to
stay home through May 26.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.310
It's the latest in a growing debate

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.710
around efforts to slow
the spread of the virus

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:26.420
while not constricting the economy.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.020
Republican leaders argue
they weren't consulted

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.530
about the decision and that
restrictions should be eased

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.200
in rural counties where
there are few cases.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.510
The governor's
administration says the order

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.360
has slowed the spread of the infection

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.960
and prevented deaths.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.040
Meanwhile, Attorney General William Barr

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.420
said the Department of Justice

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.180
would consider supporting
those who alleged their rights

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.240
had been violated by the
strict lockdown measures.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.840
Netflix scored 16 million new subscribers

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.100
in the first quarter of 2020.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.010
That's more than double

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.810
what the company had forecast

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.990
but the streaming giant
said the breakneck pace

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.790
of growth was unlikely to continue.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.880
Its stock is up 34% year to date,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.560
making the company one of the few

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.594
to see shares appreciate
during the coronavirus crisis

00:02:13.594 --> 00:02:16.160
as people stuck at home around the globe

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.590
are turning to streaming
services for entertainment.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.900
Most of the growth is from
outside of North America.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.140
Netflix has a challenge ahead of it.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.280
Practically all of its content production

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.123
has ground to a halt due to the pandemic.

